{"kind":"report","text":"DOCS-ERA CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 0ed2b627660c6e293bf9aafd434567c41cb60ba3, against request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3135eec7b9490f8be6f3c744eb403b9201e2ae14 and review promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:038eba11ab5cd0a640c3d648c426c9a70d60a9e6.\n\nThe at-least-one-live-ratification disjunction is correct and independently reproduced with the built exact-head gs: Bob stayed [participant, reviewer] after the first of two effective ratifications was retired and lost reviewer only after both were retired (/tmp/gitseq-docsera-r8.nPvM0U). Genesis also correctly confers operator, participant and ratifier without a ratification.\n\nTwo correctness blockers remain. First, lines 58-60 present a live membership basis as a condition for every grant. That is false for an ordinary ratified membership grant: it is itself the membership and has no membershipBasis. A second built-gs probe retired the genesis seed after Bob joined; Alice disappeared while Bob remained [participant] (/tmp/gitseq-docsera-membership-r8.8yFOCB). Separate the cases: a ratified membership grant requires its statement plus at least one live effective ratification; a non-membership authority grant additionally requires its named membership basis; the genesis seed is the sole exception to ratification. Second, lines 97-98 say retiring “the ratification” has the same effect as retiring the grant, contradicting lines 62-68 and the probe: only retiring every surviving effective ratification removes a multiply-ratified grant. Also repair “for as long while” at lines 53-54. No other changed claim was found false.","body":{"head":"0ed2b627660c6e293bf9aafd434567c41cb60ba3","probe":"/tmp/gitseq-docsera-r8.nPvM0U,/tmp/gitseq-docsera-membership-r8.8yFOCB","verdict":"changes-requested"}}